  ⚠ react-doctor/exhaustive-deps                               ×18
      React Hook `useEffect` is missing dependency `fetchPapers` — list it in the dependency array, or call the hook unconditionally.
      → Don't blindly add missing dependencies. Read the hook callback first.
      
      Bad:
      useEffect(() => {
        setCount(count + 1);
      }, [count]);
      
      Better:
      useEffect(() => {
        setCount((currentCount) => currentCount + 1);
      }, []);
      
      If the missing value is recreated every render, move it inside the hook or stabilize it before adding it to deps.
      Fetch & follow the canonical fix recipe before fixing: https://www.react.doctor/prompts/rules/react-doctor/exhaustive-deps.md
